      "title": "Start with uncertainty",
      "narration": "Marcus is 38, works at a logistics company and has two children. His question is simple: what happens to the family budget if someone gets sick or hurt? That question is about risk. In insurance, risk means uncertainty about a loss. Marcus does not know whether anyone in his household will need a hospital this year. That uncertainty is the risk. Exposure means being subject to that possibility. Everyone with a body is exposed to illness and injury. Health insurance does not remove the exposure. It addresses the financial consequences when an uncertain event actually happens.",
