      "title": "Peril and hazard are not the same",
      "narration": "A peril is the cause of a loss. In health insurance the perils are sickness and accidental injury. A hazard is a condition that increases the chance of a loss or makes it worse. Icy front steps are a physical hazard. Dishonesty, such as exaggerating a claim, is a moral hazard. Carelessness that grows because a person feels covered, like skipping a seatbelt, is a morale hazard. When a question describes a condition that raises the odds, it is describing a hazard. When it names the event that actually caused the bills, it is naming the peril.",
